    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "There is only one test class in the project (`AcceptanceTest`), and both its tests pass with `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec required `contactPreference` = `EMAIL` when an owner has an email, otherwise `PHONE`, returned on the owner response.\n\nI made two minimal, low-impact changes:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `contactPreference` string property to the `Owner` schema (alongside the existing computed fields like `locality`/`membershipLevel`), so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field.\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a single `@Mapping` to the existing `toOwnerDto` method with an inline expression:\n   ```java\n   @Mapping(target = \"contactPreference\",\n       expression = \"java(owner.getEmail() != null ? \\\"EMAIL\\\" : \\\"PHONE\\\")\")\n   ```\n\nI deliberately used an inline expression rather than adding a new helper method, keeping the change to one annotation on the simplest method in the class (CC 1) and avoiding any growth in surrounding complexity \u2014 this follows the same pattern already used for `displayName`, `initials`, and `locality`.",
